@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF

title WF-5: Session Management (v3.3 - CURRENT IMPLEMENTATION)

participant "User\n(Browser/App)" as U #D5E8D4
participant "Core App" as CA #DAE8FC
database "core-db" as CDB #F5F5F5

    10|== Create Session ==

note over U, CDB
  Session được tạo sau khi:
  1. Login thành công (WF-1)
  2. MFA verify thành công (WF-4)
end note

U -> CA : **POST /api/v1/auth/login**\n(username, password)
activate CA

CA -> CDB : SELECT user WHERE username
activate CDB
CDB --> CA : user record
deactivate CDB

CA -> CDB : INSERT sessions\n(token_jti, access_token_hash,\nrefresh_token_hash, expires_at=NOW()+1h,\nip_address_id, user_agent)
activate CDB
deactivate CDB

    CA --> U : **200 OK**\n{access_token, refresh_token}
    deactivate CA

== Token Refresh ==

note over U, CA
  **Refresh semantics (v3.3):**
  - Opaque tokens: NO signature, NO embedded exp/jti claims
  - Refresh rotates both access and refresh token values
  - Does NOT extend session.expires_at (fixed at login time + 1h)
  - Refresh only valid while backing session is unexpired AND not revoked
  - P1-F: concurrent refresh hardening — IMPLEMENTATION BACKLOG
end note

U -> CA : **POST /api/v1/auth/refresh**\n(refresh_token)
activate CA

CA -> CDB : SELECT session\nWHERE refresh_token_hash=?\nAND revoked_at IS NULL\nAND expires_at >= NOW()
activate CDB
CDB --> CA : session record
deactivate CDB

alt refresh_token VALID + unexpired + not revoked
    CA -> CA : Generate new opaque access_token\n(token_jti rotates)
    CA -> CDB : UPDATE sessions\n(access_token_hash=hash(new_access),\nrefresh_token_hash=hash(new_refresh),\ntoken_jti=rotation_id,\nlast_activity_at=NOW())\nNOTE: expires_at UNCHANGED
    activate CDB
    deactivate CDB
    
    CA --> U : **200 OK**\n{access_token, refresh_token}
    deactivate CA

else expired/revoked
    CA --> U : **401 TOKEN_EXPIRED**\n{relogin_required: true}
    deactivate CA
end

== Logout ==

U -> CA : **POST /api/v1/auth/logout**\n(access_token)
activate CA

CA -> CA : get_current_auth_context() → ctx.session
CA -> CDB : UPDATE sessions\n(revoked_at=NOW())\nWHERE id=ctx.session.id
activate CDB
deactivate CDB

CA -> CDB : INSERT audit_logs\n(action="logout", actor_id)
activate CDB
deactivate CDB

CA --> U : **200 OK**\n{status: "ok"}
deactivate CA

== List Active Sessions ==

U -> CA : **GET /api/v1/sessions**\n(access_token)
activate CA

CA -> CDB : SELECT sessions\nWHERE user_id=current_user_id\nAND revoked_at IS NULL\nORDER BY last_activity_at DESC
activate CDB
CDB --> CA : [session1, session2, ...]
deactivate CDB

CA --> U : **200 OK**\n{sessions: [{id, device, ip,\nlast_activity, created_at}]}
deactivate CA

== Revoke Own Session ==

U -> CA : **DELETE /api/v1/sessions/{id}**\n(access_token)
activate CA

CA -> CDB : SELECT session WHERE id=? AND user_id=current_user_id
activate CDB
CDB --> CA : session record
deactivate CDB

alt session belongs to current_user
    CA -> CDB : UPDATE sessions\n(revoked_at=NOW())\nWHERE id=? AND user_id=current_user_id
    CA --> U : **204 No Content**
    deactivate CA
else session not found or not owned
    CA --> U : **404 Not Found / 403 Forbidden**
    deactivate CA
end

note over U, CA
  **APPROVED DESIGN / IMPLEMENTATION PENDING:**
  - Logout All (revoke all sessions at once)
  - Admin Revoke (Security Admin revokes other user's session)
  - Background middleware last_activity_at update
end note

== Session Expiry Check (Bearer Token Validation) ==

note over U, CA
  **Opaque Token Validation Pipeline (v3.3):**
  1. Client sends access_token (Bearer header)
  2. API computes SHA-256 hash of token value
  3. Lookup session WHERE access_token_hash=? AND revoked_at IS NULL
  4. Check session.expires_at > NOW()
  5. If expired → 401, client uses refresh_token
  6. Or user must re-login
end note

alt Token expired
    U -> CA : Request with expired access_token
    activate CA
    CA --> U : **401 TOKEN_EXPIRED**\nWWW-Authenticate: Bearer realm="access_token"
    deactivate CA
    
    U -> CA : **POST /api/v1/auth/refresh** (refresh_token)
end

@enduml
